{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"MERGED. Both changes landed on main via plain Gerrit Submit with no rebase (the\nmerged tip is the exact SHA that was tested):\n- change 1220 -> 8961f12664 'd067: extract DC transition cluster'\n- change 1221 -> 2ea5c3391d 'd067: route DC outbound status to a transition'\nBoth carried LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero unresolved comment threads.\n\nLanded content verified against 'git fetch gerrit main':\n- transport.py:280 'status = kwargs.pop(\"status\", _MISSING)'\n- transport.py:287 'route_status_to_transition(self._client, remote_id, str(status))'\n- transitions.py present, 166 LOC\n- no @pytest.mark.xfail remains in\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200.py (the two\n  remaining 'xfail' hits are prose in docstrings recording that the marker was removed)\n\nSuites run before push: 1826 passed (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler), 35 passed\n(tests/integration/rebar_reconciler), 49 live-DC tests collect cleanly.\n\nAC status\n- [x] update_issue pops status and routes it through the transition resolver, never\n      through issue.update(fields=...)\n- [x] remaining allowlisted fields still field-edited in the same call; assignee\n      routing unchanged (test_a_status_and_an_editable_field_are_both_applied_in_one_call)\n- [x] xfail(strict=True) marker removed and the test passes asserting\n      transitioned == [('DIG-1', '11')]\n- [x] characterization test inverted, not deleted or relaxed, with the reason in its\n      docstring (test_the_dc_transport_never_edits_status_as_a_field)\n- [x] illegal transition stays non-fatal AND is observable as a bridge alert, asserted\n      through the real applier._apply_one sequencer\n- [x] [operator-attested] mutation-checked -- verdict recorded in the previous comment\n- [ ] [operator-attested] live J11 cell test_outbound_mutation_round_trips[04-transition-status]\n      GREEN on a real DC harness run. STILL OUTSTANDING: the most recent 'Live External\n      Integration' GHA run (30763838558) is on 144bb02251, which predates this merge, so\n      no post-fix harness run exists yet. A run on 2ea5c3391d or later is needed before\n      this box can be ticked."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785700927589933001,"uuid":"7e09483c-d71d-46d5-aa00-f53cd52f10c2"}